# VPN_SWITCH_DNS_UPDOWN_openvpn - Control OpenVPN's built-in dns-updown hook
#
# Optional value for the "dns-updown" directive in patched OpenVPN
# configs. OpenVPN >= 2.7 ships a built-in DNS integration (on FreeBSD
# a shared /usr/local/libexec/openvpn/dns-updown script) that would
# compete with vpn-switch's DNS phase for resolv.conf ownership.
#
# Default: (empty - no "dns-updown" directive is added)
#
# If set, vpn-switch patches configs at connect time:
#   - Existing "dns-updown" directives are rewritten to this value
#   - If no "dns-updown" directive exists, one is appended
#
# Recommended value on OpenVPN >= 2.7:
#   disable
#
# Caveat:
#   The "dns-updown" directive is unknown to OpenVPN 2.6 and earlier
#   and would make the daemon fail to start - hence opt-in, no default.
